WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:04.610
Being nominated for the New Artist 
Award is an amazing achievement.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:09.160
I finally made it this far, 
so why aren't I happy?

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.660
Maybe it's not my dream anymore.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.450
The Zero Arena...

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.460
Zero, did the same thing happen to you?

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.470
Did singing stop being your dream?

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.290
Tenn-nii!

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.210
Riku.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.210
Resolve At Zero

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.180
Disbanded...

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.360
I finally got a hold of my dream.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.740
I should be happy.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.420
So why?

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.160
Didn't I want to become like Zero?

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.940
Mitsuki.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.770
Nagi, Sogo.

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:56.450
I unconsciously headed this way.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:57.950
Me, too.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:04.650
This was where Iori cried
 after <i>Music Festa</i>.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.810
My heart hurt.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.160
You're right.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.380
It was hard, but we believed we'd 
manage as long as we were together.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.630
You're right.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:19.260
Can we not go back?

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:25.640
Has what makes us happy and 
is important to us changed?

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:30.170
I wasn't trying to become an idol at first.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.480
I just wanted my brother's 
dream to come true.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:43.240
But as I secretly helped manage the group, 
I came to like this job and IDOLiSH7.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:45.090
You're right.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:48.370
When I nearly left during the audition,

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:55.240
I never imagined that I'd come to love
 you guys and singing so much.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:59.780
So why can't I enjoy it?

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:05.550
I didn't really care about 
popularity or rules.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.380
After all, I had a goal.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:13.780
But seeing the guys work so 
hard made me want to try, too.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.390
When I hurt them, I regretted it 
from the bottom of my heart.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:25.090
When I saw them being so amazing, I got angry,
 then frustrated, but now I admire them.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.200
I know what you mean.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.740
You guys wouldn't understand.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.920
You've always been winners.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.160
I'm just posturing.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:37.170
I'm actually lame, cowardly, and pathetic.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:41.010
But I don't put up a front for myself.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.390
It's for a moment's dream.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:47.620
Sometimes I want to come totally clean.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.670
But at the same time, I don't 
want anyone to see that weakness.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.060
That's how I feel.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.230
Why?

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.630
It's not that I want to be loved.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:04.070
I want my singing and dancing to 
be loved, as a part of TRIGGER.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.720
Praising me when I fail because they love me.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.110
Disparaging me when I succeed 
because they hate me.

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:14.130
I want people to go beyond those feelings, 
and love my singing and dancing.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:18.280
I always hope it'll happen so 
I can be proud of this strength

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.580
I worked so hard to achieve.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.350
Um, what were you doing here?

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:33.520
Are you on your way back from work?

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:37.520
Your throat will get cold 
if you walk around at night.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.630
It's gotten a lot better.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.070
I've been getting fewer attacks.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.320
I see.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:49.240
It's too bad TRIGGER didn't 
get to perform the other day.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:54.330
Since I sang better than usual, 
I wanted you to see it.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:03.970
I wanted to sing like you, 
but not just to copy you.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:13.350
Because I couldn't run around outside, 
you'd sing and jump around to entertain me.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:18.110
Whenever I saw you smile, I smiled.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.360
I wanted <i>you</i> to smile, too.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:26.440
Guys...

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:31.690
Gaku-san?

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.440
Ah, so you're here, too.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.760
They all want the same thing.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:44.800
Over there.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:52.730
You guys!

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.840
Have you ever seen us perform?

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:58.730
Yes.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.100
What did you think?

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:03.930
TRIGGER was so cool and perfect.

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:07.110
The overwhelming aura you 
gave off was fantastic.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:11.020
I felt pure respect and emotion.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:14.620
I thought I was lucky to have 
seen something so wonderful,

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.120
and now I can say that with pride.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.380
It's like when you look up at a rainbow.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:25.670
My dream is for IDOLiSH7 
to surpass that rainbow.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.170
You...

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:36.400
IDOLiSH7 will surpass TRIGGER, so please, 
stay within our reach so we can overtake you.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.810
That's quite a thing to say.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.200
We won't lose, either.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.160
We're TRIGGER.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:44.990
We're ready to meet you.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:52.320
I won't ask why you left us anymore.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:55.810
I lost my personal star,

00:05:55.810 --> 00:06:00.000
but I gained an incredible rival 
that I can brag about to the world.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.130
Kujo Tenn, that's you.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.640
Sometimes, liking or admiring something 
isn't enough to make progress.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:09.110
Some things can't be overcome with kindness.

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:12.620
But I want to keep singing!

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.320
This is my weapon, after all.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:19.170
As long as I have my weapon and my friends, 
I want to keep fighting as long as I can!

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:20.830
Riku...

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.570
I'll run towards you as fast as I can.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:25.650
I'll keep running until 
I can't breathe anymore!

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:30.930
Sure. Come at me with all you've got.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:34.330
I'll forget that I had a brother
 who couldn't run.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:37.960
Nice to meet you, IDOLiSH7's Nanase Riku.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:45.500
Nice to meet you, TRIGGER's Kujo Tenn-san.

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:47.420
Very good.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.860
Bye-bye.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:00.230
Guys... and Manager.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:01.980
What are you doing?

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.850
We happened to pass by.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:06.780
We came to get you.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:09.250
Why?

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:11.490
Wait a minute, did you hear all of that?

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:18.120
As long as we're all here,

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.960
why don't we think of ways to beg the 
president for forgiveness over some ramen?

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:24.330
I agree.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:26.470
I want pork bone broth.

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:28.370
I want bonito broth.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:30.010
I'll secretly expense it.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:33.190
Then I guess we'll have 
to go bar hopping again.

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:35.550
But won't that put us over our calorie limit?

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.770
We just have to exercise to make up for it.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.550
Chashu ramen!

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:42.250
With a side of fried rice!

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:43.380
Boiled eggs.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:44.680
I want pot stickers!

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.680
You can't have pot stickers without beer.

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:49.650
Maybe I'll get a super spicy tantanmen.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.740
You think the president will forgive us?

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:08.300
He was pretty mad.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:13.050
He probably dissolved the
 group because he didn't think

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.590
we deserved to sing right now.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:16.660
What does that mean?

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:21.640
I think he just values our songs that much.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.640
IDOLiSH7's songs...

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:26.370
We never learned who was writing them.

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:28.980
I know.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:32.930
I know who composed our songs.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:33.740
What?!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:39.160
I'm the one who secretly sent IDOLiSH7's 
songs to Takanashi Productions.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:40.470
You were?!

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:43.040
Nagicchi, you wrote them?

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:47.240
No, my friend wrote them.

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:48.670
Your friend?

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:54.970
My friend wrote songs for a certain person.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:09:00.100
He came to my country to find that person.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:04.230
My friend's name is Sakura Haruki.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:07.150
Sakura Haruki? You don't mean...

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:10.610
Yes. The person who wrote Zero's songs.

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:11.860
Zero's songs?

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:16.330
So we've been singing songs 
written by Zero's composer?

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:18.620
Wow...

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:22.910
Haruki played many, many songs for me.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.990
But Haruki became sick.

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:29.960
I wanted Haruki to get better, but...

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:35.670
Not wanting to inconvenience me, 
he left behind a letter and those songs.

00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:42.850
His letter asked me to give the songs to 
someone who would sing them with care.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:49.130
I wanted them to be sung by
 a Japanese idol like Zero,

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:51.650
but no such idol existed.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:56.930
So without a word, I sent the songs to 
a company president Haruki had praised.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:58.910
He praised my father?

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.040
He said he cherished people and songs.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:05.830
After sending the songs, I wanted to 
see what the president looked like,

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.280
so I came to Japan.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:10.080
Then I was suddenly scouted.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:14.000
It really was sudden when he scouted us.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.930
I felt it was my destiny.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.610
That's how I became an idol.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:22.900
The president still doesn't know you 
were the one who sent the songs?

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:31.150
Yes. If we tell him we'll sing Haruki's 
songs with care, I'm sure he'll forgive us.

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:32.770
You're right.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:36.440
If he won't forgive us, 
I'll demand he return them.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.280
Don't ruin an emotional moment like that.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:44.610
Let's apologize and ask him to forgive us 
for not being happy about being nominated

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:45.910
for the New Artist Award.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:49.330
Should we practice our happy reactions?

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:52.210
That's not what he's angry about.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.380
Yes?

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.000
Sir!

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:59.320
Could you come with me?

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:02.880
This place...

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:06.010
It's where we held our 
first street performance.

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:12.310
Could I get a CD?

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.730
Yes. Thank you.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.110
Here you go.

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:19.770
You have my support.

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:20.900
Can I shake your hand?

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:22.720
Y-Yes.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:23.850
Thank you.

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.850
There are many here who
 haven't achieved their

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:31.960
dreams yet, just like you hadn't.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:31.620
All right!

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:37.710
You're standing on the stage 
they'd die to stand on.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:41.820
You mustn't forget what a blessing that is.

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:42.840
Yes, sir.

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:50.930
You should take better care of both 
yourselves, and the dream you once had.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:56.520
You should pat yourselves on the 
back for achieving that dream.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:01.810
I'll tell you one more time: you've been 
nominated for the New Artist Award.

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:04.780
How do you feel right now, Nanase Riku-kun?

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:06.030
I'm happy.

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:07.660
Nikaido Yamato-kun.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:11.120
We've achieved something amazing.

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:15.330
That's right. You've done something amazing.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:18.800
You're doing something so amazing, 
it can't be erased by unkind words

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:21.020
or sad misunderstandings.

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:21.920
Sir.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:27.330
You don't have to doubt the hard work 
you've been putting in for months now.

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:28.220
Yes.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.700
I'm proud of you.

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.480
You should be proud of yourselves.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:33.480
Yeah.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:35.520
Yes, sir.

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:40.150
Congratulations. That's 
all I have to say to you.

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:44.070
No way...

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.950
IDOLiSH7?

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:49.940
Excuse me—

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:54.290
Oh, uh... yeah, that's us.

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:58.380
Y-You were nominated for 
the JIMA New Artist Award.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:12:59.800
Congratulations!

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:00.710
Yeah...

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:03.340
Yeah, thanks!

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.350
We hope you win the award!

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:07.410
And perform at <i>Black or White</i>!

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:13.340
Um, my mom bought a new HDD since you'll
 be on TV a lot over the end of the year!

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:16.390
Mine, too! We'll record all your hard work!

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:20.990
Oh, I'm sorry for springing this on you!

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:22.530
Sorry for telling you what to do!

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:25.200
Thanks. We'll do our best.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:28.070
We wouldn't want those 
HDDs to go to waste.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:32.660
We'll win the JIMA New Artist Award 
for you beautiful young ladies.

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:36.710
And we'll knock TRIGGER 
out at <i>Black or White</i>.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:39.040
We hope you'll continue supporting us.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.210
We will!

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:41.570
I'm glad.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:45.670
I'm glad we were nominated and 
have the support of our fans.

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:48.720
I'm glad to be a part of IDOLiSH7.

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:53.950
Take care.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:56.580
They seemed so happy.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:14:00.360
Yeah, but we're the ones 
who are really happy.

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:03.720
All right. I'm counting on you, Ryu.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:05.010
Don't worry.

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:07.640
If it looks like you're going 
to hit him, I'll stop you.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:13.030
I don't care if it turns into a fistfight, 
but let me say what I want to say first.

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:16.250
Your lectures take two hours.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:23.380
What do you think you're doing?

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:26.500
What are we doing? We're going on strike.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:29.140
Promise you'll stop using 
underhanded techniques.

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:31.220
We won't let you leave until you do.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:33.080
You idiots!

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:36.330
Security. Hey. Hey!

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:40.150
Uh, oh. I was playing with 
scissors and cut the phone cord.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:41.900
Someone!

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.960
No one's in the office.

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:46.840
We threw them a thank you 
party with our pocket money.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:49.210
They're having fun complaining 
about you right now.

00:14:49.210 --> 00:14:50.740
Don't get ahead of yourselves!

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.800
You're not my son!

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.830
I could replace you in a heartbeat!

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:57.700
I'm gon' scalp that brainless head, ya moron!

00:14:58.170 --> 00:14:59.000
Huh?

00:14:59.000 --> 00:14:59.920
What was that?

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:05.000
Excuse me. Please continue.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:08.510
<i>Higurashi Chemical Co. 
makes your day comfortable.</i>

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:10.260
Huh?

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:13.210
<i>Melt freezing snow...</i>

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:14.510
<i>...with blazing heat.</i>

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:18.180
<i>TRIGGER.</i>

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.010
TRIGGER New Song Preview

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:24.070
Yaotome-san certainly is 
good at promoting talent.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:25.110
Ogami-san.

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:29.860
Everyone stops moving when 
this commercial plays.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.700
I'm sure their new song will do well.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:37.800
It's nearly caught up to Re:vale's 
single on pre-orders alone.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:40.490
Views

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:40.490
Up Next
[IDOLiSH7] Outdoor Concert

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:40.490
TRIGGER New Song Preview

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:40.500
It's officially starting.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.360
We can't let them beat us.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:45.630
I'm glad Mr. Shimooka-san forgave us.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:48.310
Yes. They promised to perform a party trick

00:15:48.310 --> 00:15:50.800
at the end of year party 
he's throwing at his house.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:56.220
His year-end parties are like an 
entertainment industry all-star event.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:59.790
He really adores the boys.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:01.350
What's that image?

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:04.380
TRIGGER New Song Preview

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:04.380
Up Next:
 [IDOLiSH7] Outdoor Concert

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:06.170
It's the video of their 
disastrous first concert.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:07.100
[IDOLiSH7] Outdoor Concert

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:07.100
Views

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:07.100
Up Next: 
 [IDOLiSH7] Outdoor Concert

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:09.410
What? The views...

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:12.950
Yes. For some reason, it's popular overseas.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.260
Really?

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:17.730
By the way, where is everyone today?

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:23.210
<i>Which group will win the New Artist Award?</i>

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:30.210
Who will win?!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:29.000
<i>The winner of the 12th annual Japan Idol 
Music Awards New Artist Award is...</i>

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.210
<i>TRIGGER!</i>

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:32.220
TRIGGER wins New Artist Award!!

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:35.230
<i>Kujo-san, tell us how you feel.</i>

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:59.700
TRIGGER wins New Artist Award!!

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:38.270
<i>I'm so happy. We have our 
fans to thank for this.</i>

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:40.140
<i>Thank you so much!</i>

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:43.770
<i>Tsunashi-san, who do you want
 to tell most about this win?</i>

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:48.410
<i>My family. My siblings 
have always supported me.</i>

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:50.310
<i>Yaotome-san, how do you feel?</i>

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:51.610
<i>Awesome.</i>

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:56.290
<i>I'm happiest about earning the right 
to perform at </i>Black or White<i>.</i>

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:59.700
<i>We'll win there, like we did here today!</i>

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:04.230
Later, TRIGGER won just 
like they said they would.

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:06.770
It's like they're straight out of a drama.

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:09.480
But they were genuinely moved.

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:10.800
Of course they were!

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:15.690
They won the most prestigious New Artist 
Award that's only given to one group a year.

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:22.140
I thought they were always where they 
are now without having to work for it.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:25.390
I watched this at home last year.

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:30.400
I had mixed feelings, since I thought
 Tenn-nii had abandoned me.

00:17:30.810 --> 00:17:34.150
But now I'm genuinely happy for him.

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:38.160
I understand how hard it 
was to reach this point.

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:42.100
I want the New Artist Award.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:45.410
I want to win the award and challenge them.

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:48.920
I want to challenge them to 
a fair fight and beat them!

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:48.920
TRIGGER wins New Artist Award!!

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:57.020
And of course, I'm nervous.

00:17:57.020 --> 00:18:01.260
Please don't. Not here, of all places.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:03.470
I get it! You don't have to tell me every time.

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:07.170
It's okay. Riku-kun, make sure 
your throat doesn't get cold.

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:09.540
The room is full of flowers.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:11.270
Mr. Shimooka-san...

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:13.560
Oh! Clara sent some, too.

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:14.070
Hey.

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:16.270
<b>Congratulations
 IDOLiSH7
 -Mr. Shimooka</b>

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:16.270
<b>Congratulations
 IDOLiSH7
 -TRIGGER</b>

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:16.270
<b>Congrats!
 IDOLiSH7
 -BNO Magazine</b>

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:16.280
TRIGGER sent flowers.

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:20.820
Can we safely assume TRIGGER supports us?

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.830
Yeah. We'd better work hard.

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:26.370
These don't have a name on them.

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:27.830
I wonder who they're from.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.330
They're nice flowers.

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:34.440
I hate to bring up the price, but I believe 
these are fairly expensive flowers.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.210
Osaka-san, could they be from your family?

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:37.820
Yeah, right.

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:39.840
There's no way they're happy about this.

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:43.970
Just pretend they are, even if they're not.

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:45.320
Yamato-san.

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:48.940
Then I'll pretend they're flowers from Aya.

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:51.400
I'll pretend they're from Zero.

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:53.820
He's cheering me on.

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.550
I'll pretend they're from Haruki.

00:18:56.550 --> 00:19:02.450
A healthy Haruki sent a gift to us,
 the people singing his songs.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:06.460
I'll pretend Tenn-nii sent 
me a gift personally.

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:08.290
That'll make me unstoppable.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:09.040
And you, Iori?

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:14.750
I'll imagine they're from my past self, 
who forgot to sing at <i>Music Festa</i>.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:16.000
Iori...

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:18.760
You're still bothered by that?

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:24.970
The mistake I made that day delayed us.

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:26.570
But it's all right now.

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:28.980
We can still arrive at our destination.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:33.830
I can still make up for that day's mistake.

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:38.360
You dummy, you've already made up for it.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:39.890
Yeah, Iori.

00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:45.730
You really reflected on your mistake, thought 
really hard about it, and worked really hard.

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:48.970
Everyone here knows that.

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:50.620
Nii-san.

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:52.950
No one's blaming you.

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:55.380
You're the only one blaming yourself.

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:58.970
MEZZO"'s debut is working well for us now.

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:03.380
You'll never last if you worry about 
every little mistake you make, Iorin.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:06.050
I wish you'd worry about yours a little more.

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:06.990
Guys...

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:09.100
Everyone's afraid to make mistakes.

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:15.310
Shadows of our mistakes 
prick our hearts like thorns.

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:21.400
But over time, those thorns 
have slowly melted inside you.

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:25.320
Tonight we'll win the New Artist Award, 
and where those thorns were—hello!

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:27.240
Confidence will take their place.

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:28.280
Yes.

00:20:28.280 --> 00:20:30.360
I'll sing properly tonight.

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:34.710
Like you said, I won't be nervous. 
I'll sing in my best voice.

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:37.250
Let's get that New Artist Award!

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:37.960
Yes.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:41.890
Okay, guys. Let's all hug Iori!

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:42.710
Hey!

00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:44.350
There, there!

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:44.990
Please stop!

00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:47.770
Don't treat me like a child!

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:49.940
It's nearly time for—

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:53.600
Let's go!

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:56.610
Yeah!

00:20:57.700 --> 00:21:02.650
IDOLiSH7 will now perform 
their song, "MONSTER GENERATiON."

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.340
Shaking your heart (Say!)

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:07.160
Shaking your beat (Shout!)

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:10.700
Racing through time

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:12.500
Jump! (High!) Jump! (High!)

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:19.590
This vivid GENERATiON with you

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:23.480
(One, Two, Three, Four, 
Five, Six, Seven, Jump!!!)

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:28.470
Even if it's a headwind Yes, We go!

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:32.060
Ignore it, raise your head, and advance

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:35.140
Drama greater than we can imagine

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:39.150
Goes on for Days

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:42.690
Let's escape the noise of the city

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:46.410
Match rhythms and Sing it! Wow wo

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:46.030
<i>Strangely, I wasn't nervous.</i>

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:52.420
How far can we go tomorrow?

00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:50.950
<i>Maybe it's because I feel our 
bonds are stronger than ever.</i>

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:54.580
For example (Hey!)

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:58.170
<i>The back of Yamato-san, who always 
pulls us along with a carefree grin.</i>

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:56.290
Starry skies (Shoot!)

00:21:56.290 --> 00:22:00.650
Even on nights when we can't see them (Fly! High! Fly)

00:21:58.690 --> 00:22:01.290
<i>The smiling face of Mitsuki, 
who always leads the charge,</i>

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:03.710
Don't worry, this song

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:05.720
<i>whether we're deeply moved or 
crying tears of frustration.</i>

00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:07.300
Will illuminate the way

00:22:06.730 --> 00:22:11.970
<i>The ascertaining gaze of Sogo-san, who 
always kindly looks out for everyone.</i>

00:22:07.300 --> 00:22:09.420
(Alright! Here we go!)

00:22:09.420 --> 00:22:11.210
Feel to the life! (Yeah!)

00:22:11.210 --> 00:22:12.680
Feel to the live (Go!)

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:14.520
<i>The serious expression of Nagi,</i>

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:16.560
With the intense pounding of our hearts

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:19.560
<i>who may seem like he's joking around, 
but loves us more than anyone else.</i>

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:19.560
Join! (Yes!) Join! (Yes!) 
This light we created

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:23.150
Won't ever stop

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:23.150
<i>The powerful steps of Tamaki, who's affable,</i>

00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:25.230
Shaking your heart (Say!)

00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:27.180
<i>honest, and pure, despite causing us trouble.</i>

00:22:25.230 --> 00:22:27.180
Shaking your beat (Shout!)

00:22:27.180 --> 00:22:30.820
It's still not enough

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:32.410
<i>The fingers of impudent Iori 
were trembling very slightly.</i>

00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:32.410
Shoot! (High!) Shoot! (High!)

00:22:32.410 --> 00:22:39.920
Pierce through, let's look 
for a Brand new WORLD!

00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:38.080
<i>As we strive to achieve the same 
goal, our hearts become one.</i>

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:41.420
<i>No one can beat us now!</i>

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:46.750
Diving to dream! (Yeah!)

00:22:46.750 --> 00:22:48.520
Diving to sky! (Flight!)

00:22:48.520 --> 00:22:51.640
Past all others

00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:55.180
Step, step we'll advance

00:22:55.180 --> 00:22:59.020
The future is in our hands

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:00.810
Shaking your heart (Say!)

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:02.810
Shaking your beat (Shout!)

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:06.360
I will deliver

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:08.120
Jump! (High!) Jump! (High!)

00:23:08.120 --> 00:23:15.230
This vivid GENERATiON with you

00:23:15.230 --> 00:23:18.790
(One, Two, Three, Four, 
Five, Six, Seven, Let's go!!!)

00:23:35.730 --> 00:23:41.440
The winner of the 13th annual Japan Idol 
Music Awards New Artist Award is...

00:23:42.970 --> 00:23:44.690
IDOLiSH7!
